 
    {{ 'base.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}
    {%- comment -%}
      Loaded after base.css, and deliberately *not* preloaded.

      `preload: true` adds a `<link rel="preload">` on top of the stylesheet
      link, and Shopify also advertises it in Early Hints. The browser then
      counts one of those as unused and logs:

        "preloaded using link preload in Early Hints but not used within a few
         seconds from the window's load event"

      A plain stylesheet link is already render-blocking and already fetched at
      the highest priority, so the preload bought nothing and cost a console
      warning on every page load.
    {%- endcomment -%}
